{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Do not fear, for am I in place of Elohim.</b> He says: You have nothing to fear, for I am one who fears Elohim — I am enslaved to Him and subject to His service. This is the view of Onkelos, who translated ארי דחילא דה׳ אנא, for the translation of יראה is דחילא — as if he said, 'I am a body of fear of HaShem.' And the ה of התחת is not a ה of questioning but a certain ה, like that which is written (1 Samuel 2:27) הנגלה נגליתי אל בית אביך. And he returned and mentioned a second time 'Do not fear,' for the first is fear of Joseph and the second is fear of famine, and from this he said 'I will sustain you,' because once Jacob died the famine returned to its former state, as I mentioned above; and this is the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:01.188162812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}